      "text": "where m(u,v) = (u2 + v2 + 1)−21(n−1). We can omit the term m(u,v) by a time rescaling of p(X). Therefore, we obtain a polynomial expression of p(X) in each Ui. The expressions of p(X) in each Vi is the same as that for each Ui, except by a multiplicative factor of (−1)n−1. In these coordinates for i ∈ {1,2}, v = 0 always represents the points of S1 and thus the inﬁnity of R2. Note that S1 is invariant under the ﬂow of p(X).",
